c6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["hacktoberfest","php","security-analysis","static-analysis","taint-analysis","type-inference"],"visibility":"public","forks":684,"open_issues":1949,"watchers":5784,"default_branch":"6.x","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Not sure if I'll get around to this or not, just jotting down some thoughts I had while rewriting TryAnalyzer.\r\n\r\n[Currently](https://psalm.dev/r/5977ed5c35) we have a separate issue message for variables possibly undefined due to a `try` block vs anywhere else. I think it'd be nice to improve this to actually show where the conditional block is in all cases:\r\n\r\n```\r\nINFO: [PossiblyUndefinedGlobalVariable](https://psalm.dev/126) - 6:6 - Possibly undefined global variable $foo\r\n  Defined in conditional on line 3\r\n    if (random_int(0, 1)) {\r\n  on line 4\r\n    $foo = 1;\r\n...\r\nINFO: [PossiblyUndefinedGlobalVariable](https://psalm.dev/126) - 9:6 - Possibly undefined global variable $bar\r\n  Defined in conditional on line 8\r\n    isset($foo) ? ($bar = 2) : null;\r\n...\r\nINFO: [PossiblyUndefinedGlobalVariable](https://psalm.dev/126) - 16:6 - Possibly undefined global variable $baz\r\n  Defined in conditional on line 11\r\n    switch (random_int(0, 1)) {\r\n  on line 13\r\n    $baz = 3;\r\n...\r\nINFO: [PossiblyUndefinedGlobalVariable](https://psalm.dev/126) - 22:6 - Possibly undefined global variable $foobar\r\n  Defined in conditional on line 18\r\n    try {\r\n  on line 19\r\n    $foobar = 4;\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt's already pretty good that it gives the line the variable was first seen on, but that doesn't help much [here](https://psalm.dev/r/ae94cc2518) (which is also broken and being fixed along with my TryAnalyzer rewrite).\r\n\r\nAlternatively maybe we should just say it's good enough and remove `$possibly_undefined_from_try`? Looking at the history I think that was added to fix #889, but there doesn't seem to be much point to having it be separate from `$possibly_undefined` besides the slightly different message.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/7679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/7679/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]